#. or announcements. They are most commonly used for Orca to communicate Orca-
#. specific information to the user via braille, such as confirming the
#. toggling of an Orca setting via command. The reason they are called flash
#. messages by screen readers is that they are shown on the refreshable
#. braille display for only a brief time, after which the original contents of
#. the display are restored. This label is for the spin button through which a
#. user can customize how long (in seconds) these temporary messages should be
#. displayed.
